food i love eating it talking about it  watching it on tv here is some delicious  kitchen inspiration  hi drew i'm jesse founder of life as a  strawberry and today i'm teaching you  how to make my favorite simple cranberry  sauce for the holidays  start by adding 12 ounces of cranberries  to a small saucepan with a bit of maple  syrup and honey this is going to help us  balance out the tartness of these  cranberries add a splash of water and  the juice of one orange slice then tuck  that orange right into the pot along  with everything else  add a pinch of salt and half of a  cinnamon stick for some great depth of  flavor then stir it all up and cook over  low heat for 15 to 20 minutes just until  the cranberries start to burst and break  down  remove the orange slice and the cinnamon  stick from the pot and if you don't love  this chunky cranberry sauce you can use  an immersion blender to smooth it all  out a little bit before you serve  this is a great make ahead recipe you  can serve it immediately or let it cool  and store it in the fridge for up to a  week or the freezer for several months  when you're ready to eat top with a bit  of fresh orange zest and enjoy  that recipe looks wow  [Music]
 

